From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.media.playback: BackgroundMediaPlayer for desktop players (6536)

foobar2000 gets its system media transport controls the way many desktop
players do: BackgroundMediaPlayer.Current, then that MediaPlayer's
SystemMediaTransportControls. Wine 10.0 had no Windows.Media.Playback,
so foobar2000 had no controls: it was missing from the desktop's media
controls (MPRIS) and the media keys never reached it.

This backports upstream Wine's windows.media.playback.backgroundmediaplayer
and windows.media.playback.mediaplayer dlls with their tests, and the
windows.media.playback, windows.media.core and windows.media.mediaproperties
IDLs (enums' deprecated() attributes dropped for this widl). widl now
registers the runtime classes a classes.idl declares from an imported
IDL (namespace { runtimeclass X; }), as upstream's does; before, those
dlls had no registration.

windows.media.mediacontrol: GetForWindow gives the same controls for a
window each time and keeps them while the window lives, as Windows does
(the MediaPlayer test counts that reference).
